projects.description:
The present technical cooperation project aims to:
- Consolidate pedagogical, curricular and educational management practices;
- Diagnoses, research and good pedagogical practices identification;
- Develop pedagogical material for all day education;
- Improve pedagogical and curricular practices;
- Develop training material for education professionals;
- Develop tools, methodologies and diagnoses to support the pedagogical management of the Secretariat;
- Identify innovative technologies, content and educational methodologies;
- Improve the Secretariat's educational programs management capacity.

Project                      : BRA/23/52/BRA (109562)  - Promotion of the Prevention and Eradication of Child Labour in Brazil					
Agreement Dates     : 14-MARC-2024 - 13-MARC-2028	
The Project's activities are divided into four areas of action: 
a) strengthening  National Commission for the Eradication of Child Labour (CONAETI) by reviewing the III National Plan for the Prevention and Eradication of Child Labour,  developing a National Rescue and Assistance Flow for Children and/or Adolescents removed from child labour and implementing a communication campaign; 
b) development of a pilot for professional learning in rural areas and the improvement and replication of the Inclusive Professional Learning Program (API); 
c)  collaborate to mitigate the risks of child labour in supply chains, initiating with the açaí supply chain; 
 d) promote greater visibility seeking to prevent child labour on Marajó Island (Pará State), focusing on the issues of sexual exploitation, domestic and rural work, all related to the child labour.

The project aims to:
- Improve and modernize school management processes;
- Consolidate pedagogical and curricular practices;
- Identify good practices;
- Improve pedagogical and curricular practices;
- Develop materials for an inclusive education;
- Develop and implement training of directors and heads of regional centers;
- Develop tools, methodologies and diagnoses to support the pedagogical management of the Secretariat;
- Identify innovative technologies, content and educational methodologies;
- Improve and modernize the Secretariat documentary heritage;
- Improve the Secretariat's educational programs management capacity.
